=== PARITY (vs web DrivingTab.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (DriveAnalyticsSource ->
    DrivingTabModel): useTranslation (P1/S10 facade) + useUnits (UnitPreferences pushed in the
    snapshot, so unit changes RE-PROJECT reactively) + the drive-analytics payload (web prop
    `data.drive_analytics`). The view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> DrivingTabProjection is a 1:1 port: web `safe(v)` = finite-or-0; the SI
    boundary conversions are pinned to web/src/lib/unitConversion.ts (convertTempFromSI,
    convertDistanceFromSI, the Wh/km -> Wh/mi *KM_PER_MILE efficiency math, Wh/mi vs Wh/km
    label); temp_vs_efficiency is the ONLY converted chart (the others plot raw and label with
    the unit, web parity); effTrend = dailyTrend.filter(safe(efficiency)>0); ZAxis bubble range
    30..300; date axis = slice(5); hour axis = `${h}:00`. ALL verified by EXECUTED XCTest.
  Composition -> seven GlassPanel+SectionTitle panels in web order: Speed Distribution (bar,
    CHART_COLORS[0]) · Trip Distance Distribution (bar, [2]) · Hourly Driving Pattern (composed
    bar drives + line distance, [0]/[3]) · Temperature vs Efficiency (bubble scatter, [1]) ·
    Daily Driving Trend (composed area distance + line drives, [0]/[3]) · Drive Duration
    Distribution (bar, [4]) · Efficiency Trend (area, [1]). Recharts -> Swift Charts; per Apple
    HIG (+ the repo's TSComposedChart) the composed charts share one value scale with a legend
    naming both series, rather than cloning Recharts' twin axes.
  Shared components -> @/components/ui (GlassPanel/SectionTitle) -> glass section panel; charts
    -> Swift Charts on the real TSChartPalette/TSChartFormat/TSChartGradient/tsChartAxes; feedback
    -> EmptyState/QueryError/Skeleton equivalents; motion -> TSFadeIn. Compiled against the REAL
    design Tokens + real Charts layer + real Motion in the SDK typechecks below.
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton panels) · empty (whole-surface friendly empty when the
    payload resolved with no drive data) · per-chart empty (web EmptyState message per series) ·
    error (QueryError-equivalent retry) · stale (chip + banner + one guarded auto-refresh) ·
    offline (cached charts + chip + banner) · content. Cached charts stay visible behind a
    refresh/failure, matching the web shell.
  i18n -> all 19 source strings resolve through the P1/S10 facade (table "DrivingTab") with the
    web English fallback: speedDist, distDist, hourlyPattern, tempVsEff, dailyTrend, durationDist,
    effTrend, trips, drives, distance, temp, efficiency, noSpeed, noDistDist, noHourly, noTempEff,
    noDailyTrend, noDurationData, noEffTrend  + 16 native-chrome/a11y keys (live/stale/offline/
    staleBanner/offlineBanner/loading/emptyTitle/emptyMessage/errorTitle/retry + a11yRanges/
    a11yNoData/a11yHours/a11ySamples/a11yDays) — ALL present in DrivingTab.strings. No English
    literal in Swift (fallbacks mirror the web `t(key, default)` signature).
  a11y -> each chart panel is a header-titled element carrying a pure VoiceOver value summary
